<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Wielder-side vehicle for UMW_Quilloned's dodge buff. (The hediff keeps its "parrying" name:
       it names the wielder's act, the way ability defs do — the trait names the hardware.) WeaponTraitDef.equippedStatOffsets is
       consumed ONLY by bladelink weapons (CompBladelinkWeapon) — silently inert on CompUniqueWeapon
       (decompile-verified) — so a persona-trait wielder effect must instead ride an equipped hediff:
       CompUniqueWeapon.Notify_Equipped/Notify_EquipmentLost add/remove this on the wielder directly
       (same vehicle as UMW_NeedlePointGrip's hit-chance malus).
       The +2 is in MeleeDodgeChance's UNFINALIZED units, not percent. Hediff statOffsets are summed
       by StatWorker.GetValueUnfinalized and only then does FinalizeValue apply the stat's
       postProcessCurve ((5,0) (20,0.30) (60,0.50)), so one raw point is worth ~2 percentage points of
       dodge across melee 5-20 and ~0.5pp above it, and nothing at all below raw 5 where the curve
       floors. Raw equals the wielder's melee skill level for an intact pawn: PawnCapacityOffset.GetOffset
       is (efficiency - 1) * scale, so healthy Moving/Sight contribute zero. +2 therefore reads as
       +4pp for an ordinary wielder decaying to +1pp for a melee specialist — the guard helps the
       conscript more than the master, which suits the fiction.
       Sized against the only two sources of this stat in Core+DLC: Nimble's +15 and Ideology
       BerserkTrance's +8. No vanilla weapon or apparel grants dodge at all, so there is no weapon-borne
       precedent to match; ~1/8 of a character-defining trait is the deliberate ceiling for a weapon
       trait that rolls on 2 of the 7 uniques. An earlier 0.05 here was written as though the field
       took a percentage and bought +0.1pp, i.e. nothing.
       The info card renders this with finalized:false (TraitEffectSummary.StatLine), so it shows as
       "+2.0" — the same way vanilla shows Nimble's +15, not as a percentage. -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>UMW_ParryingGuard</defName>
    <label>parrying guard</label>
    <description>The hand-guard lets the wielder catch incoming blows and turn them aside.</description>
    <hediffClass>Hediff</hediffClass>
    <everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <statOffsets>
          <MeleeDodgeChance>2</MeleeDodgeChance> <!-- raw, pre-curve: ~+4pp dodge. cf. Nimble +15 -->
        </statOffsets>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
